// Pull request author: swachchhanda000
// Change: new rule
// Title: Suspicious Service Privilege Addition
// Sigma ID: 75c4773e-7b0d-4221-a862-d7c5f5278a7d
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2026-09-27 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, privilege-escalation, stealth, T1574.011, T1068
// Description: Detects additions of suspicious privileges to the service which could indicate preparation for
//   EDR bypass or kernel driver loading. These elevated privileges enable loading kernel drivers,
//   which can bypass or disable Endpoint Detection and Response (EDR) tools on the compromised
//   system.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://blog.fox-it.com/2025/09/01/three-lazarus-rats-coming-for-your-cheese/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/e518ed5635f1cb438da9c24198ce30d826249df3/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_susp_service_privilege_addition.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ((FolderPath endswith "\\reg.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\powershell.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\pwsh.exe") or (ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName in~ ("reg.exe", "powershell.exe", "pwsh.dll"))) and (ProcessCommandLine contains "SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet" and ProcessCommandLine contains "\\Services" and ProcessCommandLine contains "RequiredPrivileges" and ProcessCommandLine contains "SeLoadDriverPrivilege" and ProcessCommandLine contains "SeDebugPrivilege")
